# Real-time Changelog Integration Guide

Since Xloudstudio (xstudio) is now configured to automatically publish releases to GitHub, your frontend website can pull this data in real-time.

## 📡 1. The Data Source
GitHub provides a public REST API for releases.

> [!TIP]
> **Private Repo Strategy**: Since you want to keep your source code private, the standard professional approach is to have a **separate public repository** just for releases (e.g., `Xloudone/Xloudstudio-releases`). 
> - **Repo A (Private)**: All your source code (Xloudstudio).
> - **Repo B (Public)**: Only the `.exe` and `latest.yml` files.
> - Configure `electron-builder` in your private repo to publish its assets to the public repo. This keeps your code 100% hidden while making updates frictionless for customers.

**API Endpoint:**
`https://api.github.com/repos/Xloudone/Xloudstudio-releases/latest`

## ⚛️ 2. React/Next.js Example Component
Display the latest release automatically on your website.

```tsx
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';

interface Release {
  tag_name: string;      // v0.1.0
  published_at: string;  // 2026-03-01T...
  body: string;          // Description from CHANGELOG.md
  html_url: string;      // GitHub link
}

const Changelog: React.FC = () => {
  const [latestRelease, setLatestRelease] = useState<Release | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('https://api.github.com/repos/Xloudone/Xloudstudio/releases/latest')
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => setLatestRelease(data))
      .catch(err => console.error("Changelog fetch failed:", err));
  }, []);

  if (!latestRelease) return <div>Loading updates...</div>;

  return (
    <div className="changelog-card">
      <h3>Version: {latestRelease.tag_name}</h3>
      <p>Published: {new Date(latestRelease.published_at).toLocaleDateString()}</p>
      <div className="description">
        {/* Use react-markdown to render the body nicely */}
        <pre>{latestRelease.body}</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};
```

## 🛠️ 3. How it stays in Sync
- **Local**: When you run `npm run dist`, [sync-changelog.js](file:///k:/XlouOne/Xstudio/scripts/sync-changelog.js) extracts notes from your [CHANGELOG.md](file:///k:/XlouOne/Xstudio/CHANGELOG.md).
- **GitHub**: `electron-builder` uploads the release with these notes.
- **Website**: Your website fetches the `/latest` endpoint, which always points to the most recent published release. No manual website updates are needed!
